__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.db
# ...except the one the Swift tests open. Everything else matching *.db in
# this project is a scan of somebody's music library -- machine-specific,
# large, and nobody else's business. This one is a FIXTURE: a few rows
# written by the Python so the Swift can prove it reads the same file.
# It is 57 kB, it regenerates byte-identically, and without it in the repo
# the compatibility claim is untested on every machine but this one.
!macapp/Tests/LoudnessKitTests/Golden/library.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
*.csv
.venv/
scans/
profiles.json

# Audio this tool WROTE. Every one of these folders is output: the files
# in them are copies the run produced and can be produced again, and they
# are enormous -- 598 MB of them reached the repository once, which is a
# clone every contributor pays for forever, because git keeps deleted
# files as well as live ones.
#
# The Golden fixtures below are the exception and are deliberately kept:
# five MP3s totalling 400 kB that the Swift tests decode, including the
# one carrying a GEOB frame that proves ffmpeg drops Serato's markers.
disco-final/
gained/
subbass-preview/
*.flac
*.mp3
*.m4a
*.wav
*.aiff
!macapp/Tests/LoudnessKitTests/Golden/**

# Renamed to macapp/ long ago; only Xcode's per-user state was left.
ui/
